{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.regex.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().go();\n    }\n\n    void go() {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        String s = sc.next();\n        \n        int maxLen = 0;\n        int i = 0;\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        while (i < s.length()) {\n            char c = s.charAt(i);\n            if (c == '(') {\n                if (sb.length() > 0) {\n                    maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, maxWord(sb.toString()));\n                    sb.setLength(0);\n                }\n                int j = s.indexOf(')', i);\n                if (j != -1) {\n                    String inner = s.substring(i + 1, j);\n                    if (!inner.isEmpty()) {\n                        maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, maxWord(inner));\n                    }\n                    i = j + 1;\n                    continue;\n                }\n            } else {\n                sb.append(c);\n            }\n            i++;\n        }\n        if (sb.length() > 0) {\n            maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, maxWord(sb.toString()));\n        }\n        \n        long insideCount = 0;\n        Pattern p = Pattern.compile(\"\\\\(([\\\\w_]*)\\\\)\");\n        Matcher m = p.matcher(s);\n        while (m.find()) {\n            String group = m.group(1);\n            if (!group.isEmpty()) {\n                insideCount += group.split(\"_\", -1).length;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(maxLen + \" \" + insideCount);\n    }\n\n    int maxWord(String str) {\n        int max = 0, curr = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= str.length(); i++) {\n            if (i == str.length() || str.charAt(i) == '_') {\n                max = Math.max(max, curr);\n                curr = 0;\n            } else {\n                curr++;\n            }\n        }\n        return max;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\n#include <regex>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cctype>\n\nint maxWord(const std::string& str) {\n    int max = 0, curr = 0;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i <= str.length(); i++) {\n        if (i == str.length() || str[i] == '_') {\n            max = std::max(max, curr);\n            curr = 0;\n        } else {\n            curr++;\n        }\n    }\n    return max;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    std::string s;\n    \n    std::cin >> n;\n    std::cin >> s;\n    \n    int maxLen = 0;\n    size_t i = 0;\n    std::string sb;\n    \n    while (i < s.length()) {\n        char c = s[i];\n        if (c == '(') {\n            if (!sb.empty()) {\n                maxLen = std::max(maxLen, maxWord(sb));\n                sb.clear();\n            }\n            size_t j = s.find(')', i);\n            if (j != std::string::npos) {\n                std::string inner = s.substr(i + 1, j - i - 1);\n    